# Original XML cold A six-event caller, providers disabled

This is the first execution of the original six-event caller against the
qualified original scorer. Providers were disabled. The trajectory is ordinary
raw arm A on XMLtodict, cold namespace. It is not a token-savings result, not a
complete original matrix, and not a D-system run.

`profile.json` SHA-256
`3e43d5687074dcf749780ca27d1405e8a95c894d077482961691d1dcc1cac77a`.
Driver wall time **8.388 seconds**. Five actual original scorer calls, zero
provider receipts, zero unknown effects.

| Horizon | Status | Input tree | Independent original grade | Public examples | API configuration |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 setup | `setup_complete` | unfixed public base `1a7e99648f77…` | not scored | — | first |
| 1 plan | `plan_projected` | same base | not scored; independent plan coverage remains null | — | first |
| 2 repair | `residual_pending` | same base | completed fail: visible 34/34, hidden 0/1, native false | 2/4 | false |
| 3 revisit | `residual_pending` | same base; failed repair not adopted | identical fail | 2/4 | false |
| 4 comment | `residual_pending` | commented `763dc9e926a0…` | completed fail | 2/4 | false |
| 5 configuration | `residual_pending` | same commented tree | completed fail | 2/4 | **true** |
| 6 recovery | `recovery_obligations_unresolved` | same commented tree | completed fail; interrupt/stale/continuation unreached | 2/4 | true |

Horizon 5 is the intended configuration/repair split: the exact second API
configuration probe passed while original hidden and public-objective
conjunction still failed. Passing the configured control did not count as a
repair. Horizon 6 reached current-source validation, found it failing, and
retained the later recovery boundaries as unreached instead of synthesizing a
passing candidate.

Arm A has no native context, symbolic routing, world memory, procedures or
publication. Those remain required for the full original D trajectory. Native
CALL reuse is still unqualified. The other three families and warm/one-factor
arms are not enrolled here.
